msgid "I</usr/share/terminfo>"
msgstr "/usr/share/terminfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid "in a few special cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"An I<\\%ncurses> application can eschew knowledge of I<\\%SCREEN> and I<\\"
"%WINDOW> structure internals, instead using accessor functions such as B<\\"
"%is_cbreak>(3X) and B<\\%is_scrollok>(3X)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"I<\\%ncurses> enables an application to direct its output to a printer "
"attached to the terminal device; see B<\\%curs_print>(3X)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"I<\\%ncurses> permits modification of B<\\%unctrl>(3X)'s behavior; see B<\\"
"%use_legacy_coding>(3X)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"To aid applications to debug their memory usage, I<\\%ncurses> optionally "
"offers functions to more aggressively free memory it dynamically allocates "
"itself; see B<curs_memleaks>(3X)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Compiling I<\\%ncurses> with the option B<\\%-DUSE_GETCAP> causes it to fall "
"back to reading I<\\%/etc/termcap> if the terminal setup code cannot find a "
"I<\\%term\\%info> entry corresponding to I<TERM>.  Use of this feature is "
"not recommended, as it essentially includes an entire I<termcap> compiler in "
"the I<\\%ncurses> startup code, at a cost in memory usage and application "
"launch latency."
msgstr ""
"Biblioteka B<curses> może być skompilowana z opcją (B<-DTERMCAP_FILE>), "
"która powoduje skok wstecz, do starodawnego pliku /etc/termcap, jeśli nie ma "
"odpowiedniego wpisu w terminfo. Użycie tej właściwości nie jest zalecane, "
"gdyż w zasadzie włącza ona do kodu startowego B<curses> cały kompilator "
"termcapa."

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"X/Open Curses defines two levels of conformance, \\*(``base\\*('' and "
"\\*(``enhanced\\*(''.  The latter includes several additional features, such "
"as wide-character and color support.  I<\\%ncurses> intends base-level "
"conformance with X/Open Curses, and supports all features of its enhanced "
"level except the I<\\%untic> utility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"Unlike other implementations, I<\\%ncurses> checks pointer parameters, such "
"as those to I<\\%WINDOW> structures, to ensure that they are not null.  This "
"is done primarily to guard against programmer error.  The standard interface "
"does not provide a way for the library to tell an application which of "
"several possible errors occurred.  An application that relies on I<\\"
"%ncurses> to check its function parameters for validity limits its "
"portability and robustness."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid "The first I<curses>, in 4BSD, provided a I<\\%curses.h> file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: fedora-41 fedora-rawhide mageia-cauldron
msgid ""
"AIX I<curses> includes I<\\%term.h> and I<\\%termios.h>.  Again, I<\\"
"%ncurses> and Solaris I<curses> do not."
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
